# Collection-root hygiene.
#
# This repository is public. The author's own research material is private and
# lives outside it, so nothing from the paths below may be copied, exported, or
# committed here, and nothing inside a sibling submodule's `.research-rag`
# state or bundle output may be added to the collection:
#
#   /mnt/DATA/projects/ai-and-fetishism     private research corpus and drafts
#   /mnt/DATA/projects/racism-and-borders   private drafts, notes, and sources
#   /mnt/DATA/obsidian-vault                personal notes vault
#   /mnt/DATA/zettlr                        personal writing notes
#   /mnt/DATA/agent-skills                  personal agent skills
#   /mnt/DATA/mcp-server-white-box-synthesis  separate local project
#   /mnt/DATA/draft-writing (2).zip         personal draft archive
#
# The patterns are the defensive half of that rule, for the parent work tree
# only. Each submodule repeats the same rules in its own `.gitignore`, which is
# where they actually apply.
**/.research-rag/
**/.memory-rag/
**/*.research-rag.zip
**/*.research-rag.zip.sha256
**/evaluation/*-report.json
mcp_settings.json
*.pdf
*.epub

# Superseded upstream clones.
#
# The vanilla gateway, the shared browser view, and the settings layer were once
# cloned beside the members here. Each app carries its own copy of the code it
# used, so these three are no longer collection members, and a member enters this
# repository through `.gitmodules` rather than as a working copy. They are listed
# so a fresh clone of one does not return untracked to every future status.
/vanilla-ultra-rag-mcp-server/
/ui-ultra-rag-mcp/
/config-ultra-rag-mcp/
